OL,3,GNEWSABoy to visit lifeboat stations in
OL,4,Ateacher's memory
OL,5,
OL,6,FA 10-year-old boy plans to visit every
OL,7,Flifeboat station in the UK in memory of
OL,8,Fhis late primary school teacher.
OL,10,FMegan Dryland, 35, died from a brain
OL,11,Ftumour earlier this year. At a memorial
OL,12,Fservice for her pupils, it was revealed
OL,13,Fshe had a lifelong passion for the
OL,14,Fcoast and a deep respect for those who
OL,15,Fsave lives at sea.
OL,17,FThe teacher and archaeologist one day
OL,18,Fhoped to visit every RNLI lifeboat
OL,19,Fstation in the UK, but passed away
OL,20,Fbefore her dream became a reality.
OL,23,APub: 30-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
